From ba55ee06882150de910e09b85307299b48bad9b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:49:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/47] Z 6III: the movie live-view restart -- TENC, TDEC, the
 YUV codecs, device 0x190

With the stop acknowledged, CaptureSequence's restart in movie mode
reaches blocks nothing had touched before. Each was the next stop:

- Reset controller. Route 1 (word 0 bit 1 of the set window, +0x340) is
  pulsed before TENC's init; the model took bits 1..3 of any word as a
  CPU core reset and stopped. Core bits are only in the offset-4 word.
- TENC, 0x152c0000 + 0x15ac0000 (device 0x1fb, INTID 0x10b), and TDEC,
  0x15300000 + 0x15b00000 (device 0x1fa, INTID 0x10c) -- names from the
  image's interrupt table; what they code is not known. Register windows
  from z63-tools/make_window.py plus what it cannot see: loop-indexed
  address pairs (+0x120.., +0x220.., +0x320..), the two five-word groups a
  helper fills through a computed pointer (+0x500, +0x514), TDEC's
  read-back of +0x400/+0x414, and the second block behind descriptor
  +0x10 (nikon-z63-tenc.h, -tdec.h).
- YUV_COMP at 0x15648000 (devices 0x1f2/0x1f3, INTID 0x75) and
  CODEC_DECOMP at 0x15660000 (0x1f4..0x1f6, INTID 0x77), one driver
  (0x40c71ac4..0x40c75178) choosing the base per device in each switch
  case: one layout for both, top registers and four groups of two
  sub-units each, including eight 36-bit address registers per sub-unit
  that the driver read-modify-writes as single 64-bit accesses
  (nikon-z63-yuvcomp.h). nikon-z63-regwindow.h gains a 64-bit-capable
  variant: QEMU splits the access and each half is checked against the
  set like any other.
- The sensor interface's device 0x190 ({0x15081000, 0x15084000,
  0x15085000}). The harvest in nikon-z63-sensorif.h took every
  descriptor's +8 base for 0x15080000, so 0x190's offsets (its functions
  are the ones the HAL calls with [0xa030578f8]) were filed a page low;
  they now also sit at +0x1000, and its +16 bank's at +0x4000. Found by
  sub_40C2A6BC writing +0x268 of 0x15081000. handle_offsets.py's
  --field only worked for 8 -- IDA prints #0x10, not #16 -- and still
  misses LDP X8, X9, [X0,#8] and per-branch pointers, so each list is the
  union with a branch-merging pass that follows those.

All storage, all declared: the read-only offsets answer 0 (idle, nothing
pending) and none of these blocks raises its interrupt or moves data.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
